WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.585 --> 00:00:01.845
- Enjoy the journey.

00:00:01.845 --> 00:00:04.170
Enjoy the whole step, the whole process,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.055
every day that you get up, just strive

00:00:06.055 --> 00:00:07.240
for whatever it is you're after.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.159
You can't earn what's in you,

00:00:09.159 --> 00:00:11.113
sitting back in a La-Z-Boy chair,

00:00:11.113 --> 00:00:14.600
hitting the remote control,
watching HBO and Cinemax.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.662
Intellect can describe them,

00:00:16.662 --> 00:00:18.362
but only instinct can find it.

00:00:18.362 --> 00:00:19.946
You must understand that the purpose

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:24.153
is an underlying chemistry
that makes you live your life.

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:26.104
Your kids are not going to make you happy.

00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:27.432
Your spouse is not
going to make you happy.

00:00:27.432 --> 00:00:29.463
A big house is not
going to make you happy.

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:32.614
We are busier than any other generation

00:00:32.614 --> 00:00:35.624
we have seen in the last
three to four hundred years.

00:00:35.624 --> 00:00:37.718
If you don't know who you are,

00:00:37.718 --> 00:00:40.551
somebody can ascribe any identity onto you

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:43.895
and you will morph into
whatever they want you to be.

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:46.231
If everything went the
way you wanted it to go,

00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:48.596
you wouldn't have anything to exercize by.

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:52.073
Because we are starting
every day with the burdens

00:00:52.073 --> 00:00:55.430
from yesterday assaulting us in today.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.878
I don't care whether
you're 30, 40, 50, 60, 70,

00:00:57.878 --> 00:01:00.056
there's something down inside of you

00:01:00.056 --> 00:01:01.351
that's still kicking.

00:01:01.351 --> 00:01:04.519
- He's an American Pastor,
Author, and filmmaker.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:06.841
He's the Bishop of the Potters House,

00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:08.954
a non-denominations American megachurch.

00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:11.192
He's received numerous honors including

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:13.974
13 honorary degrees and doctorates.

00:01:13.974 --> 00:01:16.040
He's Bishop T.D. Jakes and here is my take

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.553
on his top 10 rules or success.

00:01:18.553 --> 00:01:21.785
(digital music)

00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:24.790
- Enjoy the journey, not the destination.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.065
A lot of us delay our happiness.

00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:28.361
When I get to this level.

00:01:28.361 --> 00:01:29.369
When I get my degree.

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.349
When I get the kids.

00:01:30.349 --> 00:01:31.212
When I get married.

00:01:31.212 --> 00:01:32.253
I'm going to be happy.

00:01:32.253 --> 00:01:33.418
Enjoy the journey,

00:01:33.418 --> 00:01:35.225
Enjoy the whole step, the whole process.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:37.259
Every day that you get up, just strive

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:38.745
for whatever it is that you're after.

00:01:38.745 --> 00:01:39.980
You know, I'm a goal-oriented guy.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.197
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:41.197 --> 00:01:42.327
- You don't celebrate when you get to

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:44.123
the finish line, celebrate
all along the way.

00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:46.073
Celebrate all along the way.

00:01:46.073 --> 00:01:47.113
- [Steve] Yeah, man.

00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:51.367
- I know, I put in it, what it takes

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:54.367
to withstand the pressure.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.719
It's like your neighbors say,

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:58.036
you don't know what you've got.

00:01:58.036 --> 00:01:59.685
You don't know what you've got

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:02.018
until all hell breaks loose.

00:02:04.295 --> 00:02:06.678
You don't know what you can take

00:02:06.678 --> 00:02:09.925
until the pressure is
applied to your life.

00:02:09.925 --> 00:02:12.214
You don't know what you can endure

00:02:12.214 --> 00:02:14.680
until people stab you in the back

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.422
and walk away from you.

00:02:16.422 --> 00:02:18.946
You don't know how much courage you have

00:02:18.946 --> 00:02:21.748
until you've been under
fire and under struggle

00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:23.332
and under tribulation.

00:02:23.332 --> 00:02:26.052
You can't learn what's
in you, sitting back

00:02:26.052 --> 00:02:28.264
in a La-Z-Boy chair
hitting the remote control

00:02:28.264 --> 00:02:30.567
watching HBO and Cinemax.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.650
But when all hell breaks loose,

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.158
that's when you get to see,

00:02:47.796 --> 00:02:49.129
what you've got.

00:02:50.615 --> 00:02:54.431
Turn to your neighbors and
say, I'm made of something.

00:02:54.431 --> 00:02:58.043
I didn't get to see the design.

00:02:58.043 --> 00:03:00.397
I didn't get to see
the architectural plans

00:03:00.397 --> 00:03:03.095
but I know I'm made of some good stuff.

00:03:03.095 --> 00:03:05.558
I can tell by the burdens I bear

00:03:05.558 --> 00:03:09.354
and the load I carry
and the stuff I endure.

00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:12.776
I shock myself at what I'm able to take.

00:03:12.776 --> 00:03:15.995
It's to just that I shock my enemies,

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.436
I shock myself.

00:03:17.436 --> 00:03:21.083
They said I was going
to die and I believed it

00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.438
but through hell and high water,

00:03:23.438 --> 00:03:25.254
I'm still here.

00:03:25.254 --> 00:03:27.278
When I was in South Africa on a safari,

00:03:27.278 --> 00:03:29.529
I was blessed to be on a safari

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:31.658
after I taught for a group
of black billionaires

00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:34.298
a seminar about faith and finances.

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:38.374
And they detained me over
and gave me the privilege

00:03:38.374 --> 00:03:41.371
of staying out at Jay Paul Getty's place

00:03:41.371 --> 00:03:44.431
out there in the middle
of the jungle somewhere

00:03:44.431 --> 00:03:45.650
and to go on a safari with my son.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.649
It was amazing, so here I am in between

00:03:48.649 --> 00:03:51.800
a zoologist and he's giving
me all this information

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.647
about all the animals, their habitats,

00:03:53.647 --> 00:03:55.351
their mating practices, how they live,

00:03:55.351 --> 00:03:56.614
how they operate.

00:03:56.614 --> 00:03:58.506
And sitting on the edge of the jeep

00:03:58.506 --> 00:04:00.754
with a shotgun, to protect
us, we weren't hunting

00:04:00.754 --> 00:04:03.479
we were just watching, was a Zulu.

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:05.517
The Zulu says nothing at all.

00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:06.975
The zoologist explains all the animals.

00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:08.379
We visited all the different places

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:09.879
and seen a lot of different animals

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:11.233
but we had not found the elephant.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:13.049
He explained the elephant
but he could not find him.

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:17.067
Finally the Zulu stood
up and he put his finger

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.580
in there and he pointed up and he said,

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.189
the elephant is over there.

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:23.894
When he said it to me,
my head exploded, Larry.

00:04:23.894 --> 00:04:27.177
It exploded because all
of a sudden I realized,

00:04:27.177 --> 00:04:30.418
I'm sitting in between and instinct.

00:04:30.418 --> 00:04:34.585
Intellect can describe it but
only instinct can find it.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.940
And from the premise of that ideology,

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.830
I began going back through all of my life

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.651
and begin to see not only me but others,

00:04:43.651 --> 00:04:45.281
how, if they position themselves between

00:04:45.281 --> 00:04:47.417
intellect and instinct
and know when to move

00:04:47.417 --> 00:04:50.177
to which one, that next big thing,

00:04:50.177 --> 00:04:53.145
whether it's an elephant,
an entrepreneur pursuit,

00:04:53.145 --> 00:04:56.521
or raising a family,
it is simply over there

00:04:56.521 --> 00:04:58.482
if you follow your instincts.

00:04:58.482 --> 00:04:59.995
So many times you have a modicum of talent

00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:02.145
in an area, maybe just enough talent

00:05:02.145 --> 00:05:05.099
to appreciate people who are
really called to that area.

00:05:05.099 --> 00:05:07.875
It doesn't mean that
you need to necessarily

00:05:07.875 --> 00:05:10.539
go out and do that thing,
you must understand

00:05:10.539 --> 00:05:14.669
that the purpose is an
underlying of chemistry

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:16.120
that makes you live your life.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.979
It may not be, you may not have a strong,

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:19.465
let me give you an example
cause I'm messing mine up.

00:05:19.465 --> 00:05:21.176
Let me give you an example.

00:05:21.176 --> 00:05:24.405
I have talent as a musician,
I can play the piano.

00:05:24.405 --> 00:05:26.311
Not well enough to be a maestro,

00:05:26.311 --> 00:05:28.305
but I have a modicum
of talent in that area.

00:05:28.305 --> 00:05:30.312
But that was not my purpose.

00:05:30.312 --> 00:05:31.874
But many, many times we start working

00:05:31.874 --> 00:05:33.451
in an area that we have talent

00:05:33.451 --> 00:05:34.770
but it's not our purpose.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.433
I tell my kids this, you may start out

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:39.463
doing something that is not the thing

00:05:39.463 --> 00:05:41.005
you were created to do.

00:05:41.005 --> 00:05:43.303
It may only be the thing that leads

00:05:43.303 --> 00:05:45.506
to the thing you were creative to do.

00:05:45.506 --> 00:05:46.826
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:05:46.826 --> 00:05:47.866
- [Oprah] I've got ya.

00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:51.480
- So you can't don't stop at where you are

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.227
as if it were the destination.

00:05:54.227 --> 00:05:57.963
When in fact, in reality,
it may be the transportation

00:05:57.963 --> 00:06:01.467
that brings you into that
thing you were created to do.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:03.466
You have to own your own happiness.

00:06:03.466 --> 00:06:05.477
Take it away from other
people, demanding that

00:06:05.477 --> 00:06:06.753
they make you happy.

00:06:06.753 --> 00:06:08.686
Your kids are not going to make you happy.

00:06:08.686 --> 00:06:10.218
Your spouse is not
going to make you happy.

00:06:10.218 --> 00:06:11.641
A big house is not
going to make you happy.

00:06:11.641 --> 00:06:13.127
Own your own happiness and be responsible

00:06:13.127 --> 00:06:14.986
for doing those things that bring joy

00:06:14.986 --> 00:06:17.881
into your own heart, independently of life

00:06:17.881 --> 00:06:19.574
and people and money
and all of that stuff.

00:06:19.574 --> 00:06:20.701
- [Steve] Right.

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.365
- It doesn't necessarily
give you happiness.

00:06:22.365 --> 00:06:24.072
You have to take
responsibility of that peace

00:06:24.072 --> 00:06:25.983
and that joy that lives
inside of your heart

00:06:25.983 --> 00:06:27.916
and not inside of your stuff.

00:06:27.916 --> 00:06:30.616
The challenge in our generation,

00:06:30.616 --> 00:06:33.467
is it gradually through entertainment,

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:35.553
through television, through media,

00:06:35.553 --> 00:06:37.081
through every way possible.

00:06:37.081 --> 00:06:41.248
We are living in a generation
of the dumbing down of ideas.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.587
Because we have traded
effectiveness for busyness.

00:06:48.963 --> 00:06:53.130
Statistics say, yeah, someone
ought to clap on that.

00:06:55.346 --> 00:06:58.189
We are busier than any other generation

00:06:58.189 --> 00:07:00.919
we have seen in the
last three to 400 years.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:03.979
We are so busy we are busier than

00:07:03.979 --> 00:07:06.409
a one-armed wallpaper hanger.

00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:08.764
We are just busy, you'll get it later,

00:07:08.764 --> 00:07:09.992
don't worry about it,
it'll hit ya in a minute.

00:07:09.992 --> 00:07:13.772
We are just as busy as
we can be and we think

00:07:13.772 --> 00:07:16.579
because we're busy, we're effective.

00:07:16.579 --> 00:07:19.866
But I want you to challenge
your schedule for a minute

00:07:19.866 --> 00:07:24.478
and ask yourself, are you
really being effective

00:07:24.478 --> 00:07:28.287
or is your life cluttered
with all kinds of stuff

00:07:28.287 --> 00:07:31.901
that demands you and
drains you and taxes you

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:35.214
and stops you from being
your highest and best self

00:07:35.214 --> 00:07:39.403
and are you substituting
business and all the chaos

00:07:39.403 --> 00:07:42.433
that goes along with busyness
from being effective.

00:07:42.433 --> 00:07:44.409
Let me tell ya', a bunch
of scientists got together

00:07:44.409 --> 00:07:45.746
and they began to do some research

00:07:45.746 --> 00:07:49.058
and they began to determine
that 80% of the things

00:07:49.058 --> 00:07:52.602
we do are busy things
that we do in an area

00:07:52.602 --> 00:07:53.980
that is not effective.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:58.272
The average person only
spends 20% of their time

00:07:58.272 --> 00:08:01.419
doing the thing that they
are really gifted at,

00:08:01.419 --> 00:08:04.646
creative at, passionate
about, excited to do

00:08:04.646 --> 00:08:07.838
and the rest of it is all
the digital dumb stuff

00:08:07.838 --> 00:08:10.436
that we all have to do
in order to survive.

00:08:10.436 --> 00:08:12.265
Just crazy stuff that we're doing.

00:08:12.265 --> 00:08:15.251
Wonder what would happen
if we would go from doing

00:08:15.251 --> 00:08:18.039
80% of things that are
busy but not effective

00:08:18.039 --> 00:08:20.260
and 20% of the things
that are really effective.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.539
If we would switch those numbers around

00:08:22.539 --> 00:08:24.877
and only give 20% of
our time to the things

00:08:24.877 --> 00:08:28.360
that we have to do and 80% of our time

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.556
to the thing that we were created to do.

00:08:31.556 --> 00:08:34.556
(audience applauds)

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:37.825
Wonder what would happen to your life.

00:08:37.825 --> 00:08:38.831
Now thinK about it a minute.

00:08:38.831 --> 00:08:40.764
There's a lot of things
you can take from me

00:08:40.764 --> 00:08:41.680
and I would make it.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.120
You could take my suit,
I've got another one.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.713
You could take my car.

00:08:44.713 --> 00:08:45.867
I could get another one.

00:08:45.867 --> 00:08:47.112
You could take my house.

00:08:47.112 --> 00:08:48.688
I could get another house.

00:08:48.688 --> 00:08:50.855
But when you take my time.

00:08:52.284 --> 00:08:54.626
You have taken something from me

00:08:54.626 --> 00:08:57.522
that is totally irreplaceable.

00:08:57.522 --> 00:09:00.987
We take all kind of classes
for money management.

00:09:00.987 --> 00:09:02.968
We know how to manage our money.

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:04.509
We know how to pay our houses.

00:09:04.509 --> 00:09:06.865
We're working on our hair and our bodies

00:09:06.865 --> 00:09:07.945
and all this kind of stuff.

00:09:07.945 --> 00:09:09.997
We do everything except the most important

00:09:09.997 --> 00:09:14.096
thing is to value our time.

00:09:14.096 --> 00:09:18.206
It takes time to be creative.

00:09:18.206 --> 00:09:20.824
You were meant to be creative.

00:09:20.824 --> 00:09:22.329
You were created in the likeness

00:09:22.329 --> 00:09:25.373
and the image of a creator
and in that likeness,

00:09:25.373 --> 00:09:28.420
in that image you have creativity.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.720
If you had time, you would be creative.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:35.186
But in the absence of
time and with busyness

00:09:35.186 --> 00:09:36.891
and clutter and (imitates phone ringing)

00:09:36.891 --> 00:09:38.186
the phone rings, beep, beep, beep.

00:09:38.186 --> 00:09:39.189
You all got music playing on your phone,

00:09:39.189 --> 00:09:40.625
all kinds of stuff, and no
matter what kind of song

00:09:40.625 --> 00:09:42.161
you put on, after awhile
you hate to hear it

00:09:42.161 --> 00:09:44.888
cause every time you hear
that sound, you know it's

00:09:44.888 --> 00:09:48.265
somebody else wanting
something else from you.

00:09:48.265 --> 00:09:50.872
Just taking you away from what you are

00:09:50.872 --> 00:09:53.019
gifted and created to do.

00:09:53.019 --> 00:09:56.769
The enemy does everything he can

00:09:57.956 --> 00:10:00.623
to tear down your belief system.

00:10:01.543 --> 00:10:04.243
To destroy your belief system.

00:10:04.243 --> 00:10:07.270
If you open up a business,
if you open up a company,

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.528
one of the things you have is
vision, purpose, and goals.

00:10:11.528 --> 00:10:13.509
And you write them down
so that all of your staff

00:10:13.509 --> 00:10:15.371
and all of your team and
all of your customers

00:10:15.371 --> 00:10:18.454
can know, this is who I am.

00:10:18.454 --> 00:10:22.621
I am defined by my vision, my purpose,

00:10:23.993 --> 00:10:25.076
and my goals.

00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:27.609
That's my playbook.

00:10:27.609 --> 00:10:29.111
That's my creed.

00:10:29.111 --> 00:10:31.133
That's what I believe as a company,

00:10:31.133 --> 00:10:32.216
as an institution.

00:10:32.216 --> 00:10:33.369
I never will forget, several years ago

00:10:33.369 --> 00:10:35.194
I toured Nike.

00:10:35.194 --> 00:10:38.280
And if you ever get a chance
to go up there and tour,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.305
Nike is absolutely amazing.

00:10:40.305 --> 00:10:44.310
I could not find an
employee in all of Nike

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.893
that wasn't quick to
tell me who they were.

00:10:49.706 --> 00:10:52.604
They never talked about
who they were individually.

00:10:52.604 --> 00:10:54.865
They talked about who
they were corporately.

00:10:54.865 --> 00:10:56.549
They knew their history.

00:10:56.549 --> 00:10:58.665
They knew their background.

00:10:58.665 --> 00:11:02.417
They knew who they were as a company.

00:11:02.417 --> 00:11:06.091
A philosophy has so
permeated the organization

00:11:06.091 --> 00:11:08.371
that even the janitors
will stop and tell you

00:11:08.371 --> 00:11:10.380
the philosophy of Nike.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.946
You see the reason that's
important is, if you know who

00:11:13.946 --> 00:11:17.196
you are, then you know who you are not.

00:11:20.998 --> 00:11:23.942
If you don't know who you
are, somebody can ascribe

00:11:23.942 --> 00:11:27.647
any identity on you and you
will morph into whatever

00:11:27.647 --> 00:11:30.874
they want you to be and
that's what has happened

00:11:30.874 --> 00:11:32.397
with the whole lot of us, some of us

00:11:32.397 --> 00:11:35.641
have been 10 or 12
different people, depending

00:11:35.641 --> 00:11:39.524
upon who we were with because
we don't know who we are,

00:11:39.524 --> 00:11:41.864
we become whoever they want us to be

00:11:41.864 --> 00:11:44.762
and then when they leave
us, we are confused

00:11:44.762 --> 00:11:47.929
because we have no real understanding,

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:51.376
of who we are.

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:54.736
You say, well I thought
you were done about

00:11:54.736 --> 00:11:55.816
believing in God.

00:11:55.816 --> 00:11:57.318
I'm talking about believing
in God but I'm also

